<title>RUSSIA: Russia '96 industrial output falls 5 pct-committee.</title>
<headline>Russia '96 industrial output falls 5 pct-committee.</headline>
<dateline>MOSCOW 1997-01-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>Russian industrial production in 1996 was five percent lower than 1995, totalling 1,274 trillion roubles, State Statistics Committee figures released on Monday showed.</p>
<p>Industrial output in December was one percent higher than in November 1996 and 6.3 percent lower than in December 1995.</p>
<p>    RUSSIAN INDUSTRIAL OUTPUT	Dec 96    Nov 96    Dec 95</p>
<p>    month-on-month pct change	 +1.0	-5.8	+1.0</p>
<p>    year-on-year pct change	   -6.3	-6.0	-8.0</p>
<p>Note - Official Russian data tend to underreport a growing private sector in the economy.</p>
<p>--Moscow Newsroom, +7095 941 8520</p>
</text>
